# Names and paths the manual writes in code that this repository's source does not hold.
# One word or regular expression per line, matched against the whole name, then ' # reason'.
SushiRuntime/.+ # a header of SushiRuntime, which this repository builds against and does not hold
sycl/sycl\.hpp # the SYCL header of the toolchain
sushiai/.+ # a file of the SushiAI repository, cited as the example adapter and for its roadmap
cli/config\.local\.toml # a gitignored file each machine creates for its own paths
KernelFailed|DeviceLost|CompileFailed|sr_format|sized_from_device # names of SushiRuntime, which this repository does not hold
memory_allocation # an enumerator of sycl::errc
sushiblas_[a-z_]+_tests # a test program cmake/SushiBLASTests.cmake names from its module
pkg_check_modules # a CMake command
doxygen_exe # a configuration key of sushicore, the shared layer of the CLI
KeyError # a Python built-in exception
HostKernel # a class of the intel-llvm SYCL runtime, named in a link error
CaseName # a parameter name of GoogleTest's TYPED_TEST_SUITE macro
count_include_pad|channels_last # PyTorch names, cited for comparison
pad_bottom|safe_(max|floor|clamp) # named where a page says the library deliberately lacks it
v_[im]|sum_k # index notation of a formula written in a code span
